      "pausesClock": true,
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "Why",
          "criteria": "A float has about 7 significant digits; at 32,768 the spacing is 0.0039, so adding 0.001 rounds to no change, and smaller totals round the other way. The error depends on the total's size.",
          "modelAnswer": "Increment below half the float spacing."
        },
        {
          "label": "What you changed",
          "criteria": "Accumulate the exact integer pulse count and convert only for output; double shrinks but keeps the error; monthly resets still round.",
          "modelAnswer": "Integer pulses."
        },
        {
          "label": "How you know",
          "criteria": "Every meter reconciles with its pulse counter; a 10-year simulation is exact.",
